@startuml exp6_class
title Experiment 6 - C4 code level: classes and functions
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class "main()" as Main <<function>> {
  +main(argc, argv) : int
  builds 4 private layouts and 1 shared counter
  prints 5 configs and 3 ratios
}

class "PackedCounters~C~" as Packed <<layout>> {
  +at(i) : C*
  8 counters in ONE line
}

class "PaddedCounters~C~" as Padded <<layout>> {
  +at(i) : C*
  one line per counter
}

class PlainCounter <<reference>> {
  +increment() : uint64
  -v_ : volatile uint64
}

class FetchAddCounter <<counter>> {
  +increment() : uint64
  -v_ : atomic uint64
}

class Contender <<struct>> {
  +name : string
  +run_once : function returning RaceResult
}

class "private_contender()" as PrivateC <<function>> {
  +private_contender(layout, cpus, iterations, name) : Contender
}

class "shared_contender()" as SharedC <<function>> {
  +shared_contender(counter, cpus, iterations, name) : Contender
}

class "measure_interleaved()" as Interleaved <<function>> {
  +measure_interleaved(contenders) : vector of Measurement
}

Main ..> Packed : creates 2
Main ..> Padded : creates 2
Main ..> FetchAddCounter : creates shared one
Main ..> PrivateC : calls for 4 layouts
Main ..> SharedC : calls for shared
Main ..> Interleaved : calls once
PrivateC ..> Packed : one slot per thread
PrivateC ..> Padded : one slot per thread
PrivateC ..> Contender : returns
SharedC ..> Contender : returns
SharedC ..> FetchAddCounter : all threads use it
Packed ..> PlainCounter : holds
Packed ..> FetchAddCounter : holds
Padded ..> PlainCounter : holds
Padded ..> FetchAddCounter : holds
Interleaved ..> Contender : races each one

note bottom of Packed
  Packed and padded differ only in address layout.
  The same loop, the same counter type, the same CPUs.
end note
@enduml
